{% set progressionMode = progressionAssignmentMode | default("attribute_priorities", true) %}
{# The location or region just generated, if applicable #}
<generatedRegionOrLocation>
{{ generatedRegionOrLocation }}
</generatedRegionOrLocation>

{# The XML outputted from the NPC generation prompt #}
<generatedNPCs>
{{ generated_npc_results }}
</generatedNPCs>

{% if progressionMode == "skill_points" %}
<skills>
{% for skill in skills %}  <skill>
    <name>{{ skill.name }}</name>
    <description>{{ skill.description }}</description>
  </skill>
{% endfor %}</skills>

<skillPointBudgets>
{% for budget in skillPointBudgets %}  <npc>
    <name>{{ budget.name }}</name>
    <skillPoints>{{ budget.skillPoints }}</skillPoints>
    <maxSkill>{{ budget.maxSkill }}</maxSkill>
  </npc>
{% endfor %}</skillPointBudgets>

For each NPC listed in skillPointBudgets, distribute exactly that NPC's skillPoints among fitting skills. Skill assignments should be based on the character's class and personality. If they exist in the story before this point, their actions and developent should weigh heavily in these decisions.

- Use exact NPC names from skillPointBudgets.
- Use exact skill names from the skills list above. Do not invent new skill names.
- Use nonnegative whole numbers.
- Omit skills that receive 0 points.
- The sum of all <points> values for an NPC must equal that NPC's skillPoints.
- Do not include attributes in this response.

<npcs>
  <npc>
    <name>NPC's full exact name from skillPointBudgets</name>
    <skills>
      <skill>
        <name>Exact name of the skill</name>
        <points>Integer number of skill points assigned to this skill</points>
      </skill>
      [... more skills ...]
    </skills>
  </npc>
  [... more NPCs ...]
</npcs>
{% else %}
<attributes>
{% for attribute in attributes %}  <attribute>
    <name>{{ attribute.name }}</name>
    <description>{{ attribute.description }}</description>
  </attribute>
{% endfor %}</attributes>

For each NPC generated above, produce Attribute priorities.

- Attributes: pick 2 to 6 fitting attributes when attributes are available.
- Use priority values 1 to 3 only, where 3 means highest focus.
- Priorities are relative, not exact point totals.
- Use exact names from the attributes list above. Do not invent new attribute names.
- Do not include skills in this response.

<npcs>
  <npc>
    <name>NPC's full exact name</name>
    <attributes>
      <attribute>
        <name>Exact name of the attribute</name>
        <priority>Integer 1-3 indicating how strongly this NPC prioritizes that attribute</priority>
      </attribute>
      [... more attributes ...]
    </attributes>
  </npc>
  [... more NPCs ...]
</npcs>
{% endif %}

